WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:02.833
September 1915.


00:00:02.864 --> 00:00:05.778
The Great War. Supposed to end
before Christmas, the carnage drags on.


00:00:05.823 --> 00:00:08.479
In the United Kingdom, able-bodied men
enlist to fulfil their duty.


00:00:08.523 --> 00:00:10.168
Those who refuse to commit
are given a white feather,


00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:12.089
a symbol of cowardice and treachery.


00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:19.311
<i>Morning Standard!
Get your Morning Standard!</i>


00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:23.615
<i>Morning standard!
Get your Morning Standard.</i>


00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.616
Excuse me, sorry.


00:01:26.884 --> 00:01:28.786
Dad! Dad!


00:01:29.421 --> 00:01:32.291
- Henry, what are you doing here?
- My bit. Same as you.


00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:35.294
There's a good lad. Come here.


00:01:36.994 --> 00:01:38.029
Britain's finest.


00:01:38.995 --> 00:01:39.864
In you come.


00:01:45.735 --> 00:01:47.238
As you pass me get your hats off!


00:01:47.338 --> 00:01:49.274
Come on you cultural cul de sacs.


00:01:49.374 --> 00:01:51.942
Hurry up, the King's waiting
and he's paying for your medical.


00:01:52.043 --> 00:01:54.711
Get a move on! Come on!
Hurry it up!


00:01:54.811 --> 00:01:57.980
Medicals are waiting.
The King is paying for your time!


00:01:58.081 --> 00:01:59.683
Move it out!


00:02:13.997 --> 00:02:16.798
L... D... X.


00:02:21.922 --> 00:02:25.868
THE WAR BELOW


00:02:25.974 --> 00:02:27.144
Next!


00:02:37.852 --> 00:02:39.155
Nice deep breaths, huh?


00:02:43.724 --> 00:02:46.361
- Occupation.
- Accountant.


00:02:49.164 --> 00:02:51.399
- For how many years?
- Man and boy.


00:02:53.933 --> 00:02:54.800
I see.


00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:02.675
Your lungs have a definite crackle, which
I'd suggest comes from inhaling too much uh..


00:03:03.143 --> 00:03:05.345
pencil dust, over time.


00:03:06.113 --> 00:03:11.118
Furthermore there is an irregularity
in your heartbeat, genetic in all probability.


00:03:12.385 --> 00:03:16.123
But I'm guessing that,
these things you already know


00:03:16.223 --> 00:03:18.157
and that this isn't
your first time applying.


00:03:20.759 --> 00:03:23.962
I can do it sir.
I just want to do my bit.


00:03:24.063 --> 00:03:27.266
I'd say you already
are doing your bit, wouldn't you?


00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:30.901
Those at the bottom can do
just as much as those at the top.


00:03:33.772 --> 00:03:38.243
The war office deems it necessary
that every man fits a set of criteria,


00:03:38.876 --> 00:03:41.279
and I must abide by those rules.


00:03:43.281 --> 00:03:46.051
- There's no shame in it.
- I understand that sir.


00:03:46.151 --> 00:03:48.952
- But all I'm asking is for the same chances.
- Next.


00:03:57.094 --> 00:03:58.861
- Age.
- 25.


00:03:58.962 --> 00:04:01.334
I promise to obey the authority.


00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:03.434
I promise to obey the authority.


00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:06.506
Of all generals and officers set over me.


00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:09.205
Of all generals and officers set over me.


00:04:09.305 --> 00:04:11.410
And serve until the conclusion of war.


00:04:11.506 --> 00:04:13.510
And serve until the conclusion of war.


00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.445
God save the King.


00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:16.745
God save the King.


00:04:20.116 --> 00:04:22.452
- Dad!
- Well, spit it out.


00:04:23.353 --> 00:04:25.188
Yeah, they said I could go.


00:04:27.189 --> 00:04:29.192
No, you keep it.


00:04:30.193 --> 00:04:31.427
You're a man now.


00:04:34.363 --> 00:04:36.165
The Somme, 1916.


00:04:35.063 --> 00:04:37.765
Here, take this!
The phone line's out!


00:04:37.865 --> 00:04:41.769
Communications 113.
Utmost importance! Do you understand?


00:04:41.869 --> 00:04:44.306
- They're opening up again, sir!
- Go! Now!


00:04:45.373 --> 00:04:47.275
And Private, tell the...


00:04:50.945 --> 00:04:52.113
Keep going, move.


00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:04.357
Stretcher bearer!


00:05:04.457 --> 00:05:05.325
There's more coming!


00:05:30.115 --> 00:05:31.849
Hold off positions for counter-attack.


00:05:40.092 --> 00:05:43.127
- What are you doing here private?
- Message from position 23, sir.


00:05:50.301 --> 00:05:53.071
HQ! Position two-nine-nine.


00:05:53.171 --> 00:05:55.473
The infantry have failed
to break the forward line.


00:05:55.573 --> 00:05:58.343
The German trenches have not been taken.
Repeat, the German trenches


00:05:58.443 --> 00:06:00.110
have not been taken.


00:06:13.156 --> 00:06:16.526
- Number of casualties?
- 40,000 estimated.


00:06:18.428 --> 00:06:19.562
How can that be?


00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:23.533
Seven days, seven days,


00:06:23.633 --> 00:06:25.368
we threw everything at their lines.


00:06:27.436 --> 00:06:30.272
- How many shells?
- One and a half million, sir.


00:06:32.174 --> 00:06:33.642
One and a half million.


00:06:34.543 --> 00:06:38.113
And yet you sit there and tell me
it didn't even make a dent.


00:06:38.213 --> 00:06:41.283
Initial reports are,
the Germans dug their bunkers


00:06:41.384 --> 00:06:44.252
20 or maybe 30 feet below ground cover.


00:06:45.487 --> 00:06:48.189
With respect, sir, at that depth,


00:06:48.289 --> 00:06:51.526
all the artillery in the world
wouldn't reach them.


00:06:51.626 --> 00:06:54.962
- So it would seem.
- The plans are in place to pull back the line...


00:06:55.063 --> 00:06:57.464
- And lose ground. No.
- Sir.


00:06:57.564 --> 00:07:00.135
We shall not give our enemies
one foot of soil.


00:07:01.436 --> 00:07:02.370
Is that understood?


00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:05.972
To do so gentlemen,
would be to give them belief.


00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.475
And belief is one
of the most important aspects in war,


00:07:08.575 --> 00:07:11.445
belief in duty,
belief in one's own ability.


00:07:12.613 --> 00:07:17.383
- Belief in victory.
- General, we cannot sustain the line indefinitely.


00:07:17.483 --> 00:07:20.220
- We need...
- A decisive, next attack.


00:07:20.721 --> 00:07:21.621
I agree sir.


00:07:22.855 --> 00:07:25.458
The Germans know the British
are the best army in the world.


00:07:26.526 --> 00:07:30.163
Their morale will surely dip
with more sustained attacks.


00:07:31.564 --> 00:07:35.434
- Sir, if I may.
- If you must Jack.


00:07:37.402 --> 00:07:40.472
We need to be decisive,
that much is correct.


00:07:40.572 --> 00:07:44.476
But to break the German line, we need
to do something new, something different,


00:07:44.576 --> 00:07:47.044
something the Hun will never see coming.


00:07:47.145 --> 00:07:51.149
And you'd have such a thing...
would you?


00:07:52.783 --> 00:07:54.485
Yes sir. I believe I do.


00:07:55.114 --> 00:07:59.365
Merton & Fils Company,
tunnel and gallery construction, England


00:08:04.195 --> 00:08:06.230
His Lordship's waitin' for you, sir.


00:08:10.401 --> 00:08:11.268
Thank you.


00:08:17.774 --> 00:08:20.310
My answer is respectfully, no.


00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:24.413
You do realize what losing these men
would do to my production levels, don't you?


00:08:24.513 --> 00:08:27.484
Well you can see from your remittance
you'll be fairly compensated.


00:08:27.584 --> 00:08:30.719
Maybe I should decide
what you consider fair.


00:08:30.819 --> 00:08:35.058
- Understand, this is an important time of year for us.
- Indeed.


00:08:35.158 --> 00:08:36.658
Important time of year for Britain.


00:08:36.758 --> 00:08:40.062
Don't pull that king's officer rubbish with me.


00:08:40.162 --> 00:08:42.264
We're all doing our bit.


00:08:42.364 --> 00:08:43.999
So, until there's a better offer,


00:08:44.433 --> 00:08:45.167
I'm a busy man.


00:08:46.301 --> 00:08:47.569
You know you're absolutely right.


00:08:48.337 --> 00:08:49.537
We're all doing our bit.


00:08:50.505 --> 00:08:53.742
Boys on the front line,
the men and women in the forges and mills.


00:08:54.643 --> 00:08:58.145
And... whatever it is you do exactly.


00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:02.315
You know there's one thing I despise
more than the enemy, Mr. Rogers.


00:09:02.415 --> 00:09:05.553
It's those who climb on the backs
of the fallen and claim to be patriots.


00:09:05.653 --> 00:09:07.388
I seem to remember a few months ago,


00:09:07.787 --> 00:09:10.757
pompous jumped up little man
in charge of his own fiefdom,


00:09:10.857 --> 00:09:15.395
he thought he was above the war so,
we decided to give him a closer


00:09:15.495 --> 00:09:16.329
look at it.


00:09:18.231 --> 00:09:19.499
If you catch my drift.


00:09:23.803 --> 00:09:25.338
So it's a good job.


00:09:25.438 --> 00:09:27.206
There's people such as yourself,


00:09:27.306 --> 00:09:29.642
who understand that the British
need to pull together


00:09:29.742 --> 00:09:32.045
- in their time of need.
- Quite.


00:09:33.779 --> 00:09:39.083
So, I'm going to respectfully request,
that you give your country,


00:09:39.183 --> 00:09:40.486
what it bloody well asks of you.


00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.691
Once the paperwork is signed,
War Office will issue a receipt


00:09:46.791 --> 00:09:50.329
in a couple of weeks. Anything
that's still unclear, let my secretary know.


00:09:51.362 --> 00:09:55.733
I understand that this is somewhat irregular,
but I have some matters of great importance


00:09:55.833 --> 00:09:56.668
to discuss with you.


00:09:58.802 --> 00:10:00.104
I'm sorry would you mind?


00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:11.682
That's more like it.


00:10:12.816 --> 00:10:14.585
Don't let the papers fool you, gentlemen.


00:10:15.552 --> 00:10:16.786
We are losing this war.


00:10:18.121 --> 00:10:20.857
And unless we take dramatic action
I'm afraid we will forfeit.


00:10:21.458 --> 00:10:25.261
Look, that pinstripe pillock's
probably docking our pay for this.


00:10:25.361 --> 00:10:26.729
So can you just get on with it?


00:10:26.829 --> 00:10:31.400
Alright. Your country needs you.


00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:34.570
Alright.


00:10:45.413 --> 00:10:49.351
While you enjoyed those few seconds
laughing, one of our boys


00:10:49.451 --> 00:10:51.419
was hit in the head by a Fritz sniper.


00:10:51.953 --> 00:10:54.655
Somebody's father was pulverized
by a mortar bomb.


00:10:54.755 --> 00:10:58.860
And someone, perhaps a friend of yours,
had his guts ripped open by shrapnel.


00:11:00.561 --> 00:11:04.231
I enjoy a joke as much as the next man,
gentlemen, but if I may...


00:11:04.966 --> 00:11:07.434
...I would like to share
with you the situation we are in.


00:11:14.508 --> 00:11:15.409
Gather round.


00:11:24.585 --> 00:11:25.718
This is the Somme.


00:11:28.888 --> 00:11:33.760
These markers here, are the Allied lines.
This, the German front.


00:11:34.794 --> 00:11:39.831
Now, the Germans have built bunkers,
30 feet below ground level,


00:11:39.931 --> 00:11:43.469
and we've thrown everything
we've got at them, and nothing,


00:11:43.569 --> 00:11:45.404
for it's as likely
to be injured slipping on


00:11:45.504 --> 00:11:47.572
sauerkraut is he is
from one of our bombs.


00:11:47.673 --> 00:11:50.408
And of course
when the bombardment ends,


00:11:50.508 --> 00:11:53.679
up he pops, starts using
our boys for target practice.


00:11:55.447 --> 00:11:59.417
Morale in France is at rock bottom,
and with our new campaign in Flanders,


00:11:59.517 --> 00:12:03.688
we need a decisive victory,
something that will show our chaps


00:12:03.788 --> 00:12:05.556
this war is still there to be won.


00:12:05.656 --> 00:12:08.492
Sorry Bob, still don't see
what this has to do with us.


00:12:10.593 --> 00:12:14.265
With these deep hidey holes,
Fritz is a tough nut to crack from above.


00:12:15.966 --> 00:12:18.401
- But there is one other option.
- Dig.


00:12:19.836 --> 00:12:20.705
Precisely.


00:12:22.405 --> 00:12:25.642
We're going to tunnel,
under no man's land.


00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:28.410
Blow the enemy to Kingdom Come.


00:12:30.346 --> 00:12:34.850
Our initial target,
is this forward bunker here,


00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:38.454
obstinate little bastard hell-bent
on slaughtering our boys.


00:12:38.921 --> 00:12:40.823
With our first tunnels,
we've been unsuccessful.


00:12:41.757 --> 00:12:43.659
They barely last a day without collapsing.


00:12:44.693 --> 00:12:45.928
What's ground made from?


00:12:48.429 --> 00:12:49.331
Clay.


00:12:51.467 --> 00:12:53.935
Quite frankly,
we don't have the expertise.


00:12:54.569 --> 00:12:58.440
But you men do,
there's a platoon, waiting in Salisbury.


00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:01.275
Your job is to teach them
how to tunnel the clay,


00:13:01.375 --> 00:13:02.910
and how to set the charges.


00:13:03.511 --> 00:13:07.014
So, um... how long we got, sir?


00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.952
- One month.
- Jesus Christ.


00:13:11.718 --> 00:13:15.288
And then the platoon has, another three
to get the job done in France.


00:13:15.388 --> 00:13:19.292
- No.
- Well I'm sorry but that's all the time we have.


00:13:19.392 --> 00:13:20.761
I know they won't get the job done.


00:13:23.363 --> 00:13:26.433
- What's your name?
- William Hawkin, sir.


00:13:26.533 --> 00:13:27.934
Well then Mr. Hawkin...


00:13:28.835 --> 00:13:31.303
...if you've something to say
now's the time.


00:13:31.403 --> 00:13:34.807
Well I've not met that many clerks
or bank managers in me time,


00:13:34.907 --> 00:13:37.643
but I doubt any of them
can tunnel that fast.


00:13:37.743 --> 00:13:40.713
With the constant risk of collapse,
and come out the other end,


00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:42.914
we've been tunnelling all our lives,


00:13:43.015 --> 00:13:44.582
there's still always risk.


00:13:45.518 --> 00:13:48.354
No. You want your big explosions sir,


00:13:48.988 --> 00:13:49.989
you should think again.


00:13:51.991 --> 00:13:53.691
Very well, what do you propose?


00:13:56.061 --> 00:13:57.662
I propose we go in their place.


00:14:00.665 --> 00:14:02.357
- Are you prepared to do that?
- Aye.


00:14:02.557 --> 00:14:03.357
Aye.


00:14:07.438 --> 00:14:10.008
Good lads. I'll take this to General Haig.


00:14:11.009 --> 00:14:12.810
We'll get you to Flanders in no time.


00:14:14.012 --> 00:14:15.312
Thank you sir.


00:14:16.981 --> 00:14:18.649
Well you better get back to work.


00:14:35.431 --> 00:14:37.034
Preposterous!


00:14:37.134 --> 00:14:39.101
Sir if you would just allow me to explain.


00:14:39.202 --> 00:14:41.603
Something the Germans wouldn't see coming.


00:14:42.072 --> 00:14:44.407
I didn't realize that meant putting
our war effort into the hands


00:14:44.507 --> 00:14:46.608
of uneducated, untrained civilians.


00:14:47.176 --> 00:14:49.111
These men may not be soldier material.


00:14:49.212 --> 00:14:51.047
I grant you that sir,


00:14:51.148 --> 00:14:54.116
but they don't have to be,
they just have to dig.


00:14:54.217 --> 00:14:56.818
And by Jove can they dig.
Why only last year...


00:14:56.918 --> 00:14:58.987
Burrow through to Australia
for all I care.


00:15:00.421 --> 00:15:04.993
This is a military operation, Jack,
not some... some social experiment.


00:15:05.826 --> 00:15:08.362
If it goes belly up,
the whole war effort is over.


00:15:08.762 --> 00:15:13.134
- Do you understand that?
- I must confess, I too had my reservation.


00:15:14.169 --> 00:15:16.436
The infantry will break through.


00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:20.574
We just need to keep
pushing, pushing, pushing.


00:15:20.674 --> 00:15:25.012
- But at what cost, sir?
- A war of nations, is a war of numbers.


00:15:25.112 --> 00:15:29.049
We have the numbers,
and we will outlast the Germans.


00:15:29.149 --> 00:15:30.750
That's how we win.


00:15:32.086 --> 00:15:33.020
The answer's no.


00:15:34.355 --> 00:15:37.023
- You're dismissed Colonel.
- With the greatest respect sir,


00:15:37.123 --> 00:15:38.858
this is no longer the age of the horse.


00:15:38.959 --> 00:15:40.627
This is the age of the tank.


00:15:40.727 --> 00:15:43.129
The old ways are dead
and we must change and quickly,


00:15:43.229 --> 00:15:45.397
or we'll have another Somme on our hands,


00:15:45.497 --> 00:15:47.833
and the stench of blood will reach
all the way to England.


00:15:47.933 --> 00:15:51.536
Lloyd George won't stand for that,
General. Heads will roll.


00:15:51.637 --> 00:15:54.438
You have a very promising career
ahead of you Colonel.


00:15:55.606 --> 00:15:57.809
- Think very carefully.
- I already have sir.


00:15:57.910 --> 00:16:00.745
This is our best
and only option, I assure you.


00:16:01.146 --> 00:16:04.849
You'd personally vouch
for these, sewer workers...


00:16:06.018 --> 00:16:06.884
...would you?


00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:12.856
Yes sir, I would.
And if they're not up to the job,


00:16:12.957 --> 00:16:17.996
strip me of my commission and send me
to the front line, but just give me 4 months sir.


00:16:18.863 --> 00:16:20.430
You'll have all the proof you need.


00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:27.771
Very well, two months,
and not a moment more.


00:16:28.973 --> 00:16:32.142
- Sir, may I just say...
- Decision's been made, Archie.


00:16:32.242 --> 00:16:34.177
Jack and his men
will fall under your command.


00:16:34.277 --> 00:16:36.613
- Then I would like it on record...
- Duly noted.


00:16:39.082 --> 00:16:41.617
Thank you for your assistance, both.


00:16:41.717 --> 00:16:42.953
Keep me posted.


00:16:43.719 --> 00:16:47.690
And Jack, for God's sake
don't bugger it up,


00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:48.791
Sir.


00:17:09.876 --> 00:17:14.216
If you want to bring these
cave dwellers to the front,


00:17:14.316 --> 00:17:20.854
then on your own head be it,
that you keep them on course, keep them in line.


00:17:22.023 --> 00:17:24.025
And keep them out of my way.


00:17:27.793 --> 00:17:30.097
- Understand?
- Perfectly sir.


00:17:57.655 --> 00:17:59.124
Two months, that's all it'll take.


00:17:59.224 --> 00:18:00.692
One bullet is all it'll take.


00:18:01.593 --> 00:18:03.062
You'll miss Mother's birthday.


00:18:03.795 --> 00:18:06.264
She can go with me,
to scare the Boche half to death.


00:18:10.202 --> 00:18:11.070
Jane...


00:18:12.237 --> 00:18:14.838
...it's my duty, and responsibility.


00:18:14.938 --> 00:18:16.940
Responsibility
is to be here with your family.


00:18:18.342 --> 00:18:21.578
Why you? Don't they have miners
over there or some it?


00:18:21.678 --> 00:18:24.881
It's not as simple as that.
They need people who can dig the clay.


00:18:25.349 --> 00:18:26.950
They called us experts they did.


00:18:27.986 --> 00:18:29.320
I'll be useful for once.


00:18:30.044 --> 00:18:33.056
No more putting up with old Rogers
when I get back, I can tell you.


00:18:34.258 --> 00:18:37.560
The army will probably give me a new job,
a proper job. And the money...


00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:39.163
You're a bloody fool at times.


00:18:39.862 --> 00:18:42.665
There's no shame in doing
what you do, a clueless busybody


00:18:42.666 --> 00:18:44.933
- with a white feather didn't know
a damn thing about you.
- Jane!


00:18:48.871 --> 00:18:50.273
I'm not doing this blindly.


00:18:52.707 --> 00:18:54.977
Everything I care about
is in this house.


00:18:56.212 --> 00:18:57.813
And I'm protecting this house.


00:18:58.214 --> 00:19:00.349
I can't bear to think
what would happen if I didn't.


00:19:03.118 --> 00:19:04.352
I'll make you proud of me.


00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:05.988
I promise.


00:19:08.056 --> 00:19:10.891
It seems like every week
I know another wife with a brave,


00:19:10.992 --> 00:19:12.827
dead husband that she can be proud of.


00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:20.667
No, I'll go.


00:19:44.959 --> 00:19:46.059
How's the infantry doing?


00:19:49.229 --> 00:19:50.330
D'you need hand with that?


00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:53.799
Are you coming back?


00:19:55.101 --> 00:19:56.202
Of course I am.


00:19:57.036 --> 00:19:58.070
What makes you say that?


00:19:58.803 --> 00:20:00.805
Uncle David didn't.


00:20:02.741 --> 00:20:03.976
It's not the same son.


00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:06.979
Uncle David was made to do something


00:20:07.079 --> 00:20:09.647
he hadn't done before,
and it went wrong.


00:20:10.214 --> 00:20:11.082
He was unlucky.


00:20:12.284 --> 00:20:15.287
That's not like me.
I'm going there to dig, that's all.


00:20:16.021 --> 00:20:18.822
- Just dig.
- D'you good at diggin'?


00:20:18.922 --> 00:20:22.893
Aye, I am. So you see
there's no need to worry.


00:20:25.829 --> 00:20:27.898
I can't get it to stay.


00:20:29.732 --> 00:20:31.801
Let's see what
we can do about that shall we?


00:20:32.936 --> 00:20:35.704
Are you going to ride a horsey?


00:20:35.804 --> 00:20:39.944
No, I'll be in a special unit,
top-secret.


00:20:41.279 --> 00:20:42.912
I'll have my own uniform
and everything.


00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.814
- You can wear it if you like.
- Any medals?


00:20:47.117 --> 00:20:51.221
Loads of them. By the time I come home
I'll be half man, half tea kettle.


00:20:53.456 --> 00:20:54.456
There you go.


00:20:56.091 --> 00:20:57.026
All done.


00:21:10.768 --> 00:21:15.139
Flanders, 1916


00:21:15.977 --> 00:21:17.712
Let's get away, come on, get on.


00:21:19.813 --> 00:21:20.982
Move along.


00:21:33.527 --> 00:21:35.996
Excuse us pal, we just got here.


00:21:36.096 --> 00:21:38.298
Alright, good for you. And?


00:21:39.132 --> 00:21:40.833
We've no sodding idea where we're going.


00:21:41.867 --> 00:21:43.103
You got papers?


00:21:50.209 --> 00:21:52.511
Ah! You're with Hellfire Jack yes?


00:21:52.612 --> 00:21:54.947
- Who?
- Colonel Norton-Griffiths.


00:21:55.047 --> 00:21:56.116
Up in section three.


00:21:57.583 --> 00:21:58.750
Section three!


00:22:04.923 --> 00:22:06.791
Come on, I'll show you boys.


00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:10.528
Trench system is simple enough.


00:22:11.363 --> 00:22:15.467
It's made out of three main lines:
the reserve, the support, the firing line.


00:22:15.567 --> 00:22:17.835
These are the communication trenches.


00:22:17.936 --> 00:22:18.902
They connect the lines.


00:22:21.472 --> 00:22:25.477
This is the reserve.
Here you can rest up, relax.


00:22:27.312 --> 00:22:29.546
Oh aye, looks very relaxing.


00:22:31.248 --> 00:22:33.251
We're coming up to the support line now.


00:22:33.917 --> 00:22:35.953
Christ, what's that smell?


00:22:36.053 --> 00:22:37.854
- Dirty bastard.
- Oh sod off.


00:22:37.955 --> 00:22:41.257
It's a mixture of shit,
piss, cordite and decomposition.


00:22:41.357 --> 00:22:43.460
Like no other, eh. Don't worry.


00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:45.029
You get used to it after a while.


00:22:48.564 --> 00:22:49.865
Cheerio, chum.


00:22:53.403 --> 00:22:55.171
Fritz seems a bit feisty this morning.


00:22:56.039 --> 00:22:57.240
You right, youth?


00:23:00.309 --> 00:23:02.312
Don't worry. You'll get used to it.


00:23:06.381 --> 00:23:08.150
And, here we are.


00:23:11.187 --> 00:23:12.521
So this is the Great War.


00:23:17.559 --> 00:23:20.195
All the water's chlorinated.
Tastes a bit strange at first.


00:23:20.295 --> 00:23:22.531
Yeah yeah. I know, I'll get used to it.


00:23:23.532 --> 00:23:26.334
Alright thank you, captain.
I'll take it from here.


00:23:28.135 --> 00:23:30.571
Bill, glad you all made it.


00:23:30.671 --> 00:23:33.474
- Yeah.
- I think some of 'em
are starting to wish they hadn't.


00:23:34.342 --> 00:23:36.377
Well you're here now,
so let's crack on,


00:23:36.476 --> 00:23:38.144
see if we can't get you
all back to Blighty.


00:23:38.244 --> 00:23:39.080
Here come look at this.


00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:42.915
Hey Harold, I've got to go, you know.


00:23:43.416 --> 00:23:46.186
Tie a bloody knot in it.
Not hold it in?


00:23:46.286 --> 00:23:48.254
Not unless you want me
to hold it in my trousers, no.


00:23:48.356 --> 00:23:50.190
Alright, just be bloody quick then.


00:23:50.657 --> 00:23:53.259
- Here take a look, 12 o'clock.
- What're we looking at?


00:23:56.362 --> 00:23:59.933
Nuthin' much to look at is it?
But, that's our lady nonetheless.


00:24:00.033 --> 00:24:02.067
About 350 yards from where
we're standing right now.


00:24:03.335 --> 00:24:06.305
Used to be a farmhouse,
now the Boche are using it


00:24:06.405 --> 00:24:10.175
as a forward machine gun post,
they've dug in deep underneath.


00:24:23.588 --> 00:24:26.058
- Officer approaching!
- Now, look sharp.


00:24:27.959 --> 00:24:28.926
Sir.


00:24:30.728 --> 00:24:31.996
Jack.


00:24:33.530 --> 00:24:34.431
So...


00:24:35.399 --> 00:24:38.536
...this is your, little rabble then, is it?


00:24:38.636 --> 00:24:40.237
They are indeed sir. My clay kickers.


00:24:41.538 --> 00:24:44.074
What in God's green earth
am I looking at here?


00:24:44.174 --> 00:24:48.445
Get on your feet boy!
And you get off that wall [...]!


00:24:48.545 --> 00:24:51.481
Wearing the King's uniform,
act like it.


00:24:52.214 --> 00:24:54.684
Your village missing an idiot
now you're here, is it?


00:24:55.652 --> 00:25:01.090
Shut your mouth. The enemy will die,
laughing before you can shoot them.


00:25:13.202 --> 00:25:14.103
Shit.


00:25:18.473 --> 00:25:21.943
- Name.
- Hawkin. William Hawkin, sir.


00:25:23.344 --> 00:25:29.049
And you'd be in charge of this,
this bunch then, would you, Hawkin?


00:25:30.150 --> 00:25:32.287
- Yes sir. I am sir.
- Jolly good.


00:25:34.289 --> 00:25:38.091
You shall be held accountable
for their actions then. Hmm?


00:25:42.162 --> 00:25:45.032
Just keep them away
from the real soldiers, Jack.


00:25:45.132 --> 00:25:47.334
We don't want the sideshow
to become a circus now.


00:25:47.434 --> 00:25:49.268
- Sir with respect.
- Shut your mouth!


00:25:49.669 --> 00:25:52.739
You don't speak till an officer speaks to you,
do you understand?


00:25:52.840 --> 00:25:55.708
- Yes sir.
- It's not "sir," it's "s'arnt."


00:25:55.808 --> 00:25:58.444
- Yes, s'arnt.
- Sure it won't be a problem sir?


00:25:59.445 --> 00:26:00.413
Good show.


00:26:03.249 --> 00:26:05.685
- Excuse a minute.
- Mate, mate! Mate!


00:26:06.352 --> 00:26:10.056
I don't remember layin' about to you,
I don't remember goin' to school with you!


00:26:10.156 --> 00:26:13.124
- Mate? I'm a s'arnt, say it!
- S'arnt.


00:26:13.225 --> 00:26:14.392
- Say it louder!
- S'arnt.


00:26:15.460 --> 00:26:16.595
You thing!


00:26:18.797 --> 00:26:23.535
Once again, Jack.
Excellent men you have here.


00:26:24.336 --> 00:26:26.337
- Only the very best sir.
- Hmm.


00:26:31.409 --> 00:26:35.646
Some stupid bastard, thinks this lot's
gonna hold up ten tonne of shite.


00:26:35.746 --> 00:26:37.681
- I guess thinking wasn't needed at Eton.
- No.


00:26:39.817 --> 00:26:43.521
32 degrees for the first 100,
minus ten up next.


00:26:44.287 --> 00:26:47.525
- A lot of ground to cover.
- We better shift our asses then hadn't we?


00:26:48.259 --> 00:26:51.060
Wouldn't want to be
on a charge now would we Harker?


00:26:53.730 --> 00:26:56.065
You are our keeper O Lord you are.


00:26:56.165 --> 00:26:58.768
Oh knock it off lad,
think He's listening out here?


00:26:58.868 --> 00:26:59.802
It's a tradition.


00:27:02.804 --> 00:27:04.306
Go on then Saint George.


00:27:06.809 --> 00:27:09.711
Deliver us from evil, keep our souls.


00:27:12.748 --> 00:27:14.049
Shorty.


00:28:00.359 --> 00:28:01.594
<i>My dearest Jane...</i>


00:28:02.762 --> 00:28:04.297
<i>...every time I write to you,</i>


00:28:04.764 --> 00:28:07.366
<i>I fear my stories
are just a spinning carousel.</i>


00:28:08.400 --> 00:28:09.702
<i>Our life continues.</i>


00:28:10.769 --> 00:28:11.769
<i>We dig the clay.</i>


00:28:12.871 --> 00:28:14.540
<i>And the work can suck the life</i>


00:28:14.640 --> 00:28:16.575
<i>from your bones if you're not careful.</i>


00:28:18.543 --> 00:28:21.512
<i>The days when it's quiet, I forget,</i>


00:28:21.614 --> 00:28:24.182
<i>I think I'm just digging
a sewer tunnel back home.</i>


00:28:24.749 --> 00:28:26.517
<i>I think I'm gonna end my day with you.</i>


00:28:27.385 --> 00:28:31.255
<i>When we climb back up,
I remember what our home is now.</i>


00:28:31.756 --> 00:28:33.791
<i>It's strange the things you get used to.</i>


00:28:34.492 --> 00:28:36.427
<i>The rats, the stench.</i>


00:28:37.694 --> 00:28:39.830
<i>There are too many things
that I want to forget.</i>


00:28:50.307 --> 00:28:53.143
<i>My heart sinks that the other men
take us for cowards.</i>


00:28:53.677 --> 00:28:55.678
<i>That we hide from the fighting down here.</i>


00:28:57.446 --> 00:28:59.349
<i>I want them to know what we do.</i>


00:28:59.449 --> 00:29:01.318
<i>To see us as true soldiers.</i>


00:29:02.518 --> 00:29:04.353
<i>But we are once again on our own.</i>


00:29:06.355 --> 00:29:10.192
<i>The war to end all wars,
it is what I believe we're here for.</i>


00:29:11.560 --> 00:29:15.563
<i>So I shall do my part, my duty...</i>


00:29:16.297 --> 00:29:17.532
<i>...and then I'll come home to you.</i>


00:29:19.869 --> 00:29:22.671
<i>Take care of yourself, and our boy.</i>


00:29:24.339 --> 00:29:25.707
<i>All my love forever.</i>


00:29:27.876 --> 00:29:28.877
<i>William.</i>


00:29:43.925 --> 00:29:46.292
Been here two months, feel like I'm 60 odd.


00:29:47.161 --> 00:29:48.562
Ah could be worse.


00:29:49.530 --> 00:29:50.864
- How's that then?
- I dunno.


00:29:51.831 --> 00:29:53.433
Just what people say ain't it?


00:29:54.367 --> 00:29:55.468
Come on lads.


00:29:56.470 --> 00:29:57.438
Time's wasting.


00:30:28.366 --> 00:30:29.467
Aah!


00:30:29.968 --> 00:30:32.737
Fritz bastard goes for me every damn day.


00:30:32.837 --> 00:30:34.806
Who the hell wants to shoot someone
when on the crapper?


00:30:34.906 --> 00:30:35.840
Anyone who knows you?


00:30:37.708 --> 00:30:39.543
If it weren't him it'd be somebody else.


00:30:40.811 --> 00:30:43.380
Don't take it personal
we'll be out of this soon enough.


00:30:45.050 --> 00:30:48.351
- How long we got left anyway?
- 40, 45 yards to go.


00:30:49.886 --> 00:30:52.857
Get these coordinates spot on.
Light it up, we'll be on our way.


00:31:22.818 --> 00:31:23.852
And that's the 200.


00:31:24.954 --> 00:31:27.722
Alright. Dig out caverns
set bombs and job done.


00:31:34.629 --> 00:31:37.565
- Oh Jesus Christ.
- Keep sucking on it, it'll break up.


00:31:38.632 --> 00:31:41.036
It's like them things what you give babies,
but made of concrete.


00:31:41.136 --> 00:31:42.503
They're dog biscuits.


00:31:42.938 --> 00:31:45.372
You what? These are not
bloody dog biscuits.


00:31:45.472 --> 00:31:47.074
I've been eating these things
since I got here.


00:31:47.175 --> 00:31:50.777
I'm telling you.
Had staffies since I were a nipper so, I know.


00:31:50.877 --> 00:31:53.480
It's true we did.
Nasty little buggers they were.


00:31:53.580 --> 00:31:56.882
Used to good taste is all.
And this is a dog biscuit.


00:32:03.455 --> 00:32:06.059
Bloody hell. That were close.


00:32:06.792 --> 00:32:09.461
That were close.


00:32:27.179 --> 00:32:28.646
Christ it's gonna break!


00:32:29.447 --> 00:32:30.348
Brace the walls!


00:32:34.852 --> 00:32:35.987
Shit!


00:32:36.088 --> 00:32:37.089
Get back!


00:32:37.689 --> 00:32:38.924
Move now!


00:32:50.601 --> 00:32:52.636
Everyone all right?


00:32:55.037 --> 00:32:56.040
George?


00:32:56.140 --> 00:32:58.876
Yeah I'm fine. I'm fine.


00:33:01.011 --> 00:33:02.445
Charlie you okay?


00:33:03.947 --> 00:33:04.815
Charlie?


00:33:07.550 --> 00:33:08.517
No I'm not.


00:33:09.305 --> 00:33:12.021
Like we're too close this time,
too bloody close.


00:33:16.859 --> 00:33:19.028
Good job you were doing
all that praying hey, Georgie.


00:33:20.795 --> 00:33:21.796
Still alive aren't you?


00:33:23.866 --> 00:33:25.867
This what you imagined it would be like, Bill?


00:33:26.701 --> 00:33:27.970
I don't know what I imagined.


00:33:29.638 --> 00:33:30.504
Not for me.


00:33:33.608 --> 00:33:35.877
I er, got a postcard
from Maggie this morning.


00:33:37.245 --> 00:33:40.048
She said the Goose Fair
just started in town. She saw those um..


00:33:41.482 --> 00:33:43.450
...those toffee apple stalls
and everything.


00:33:46.087 --> 00:33:48.489
Y'know I used to go every year
with-without fail.


00:33:52.127 --> 00:33:53.128
Wish I was this year.


00:33:59.133 --> 00:34:00.533
Sounds like a lot of fun.


00:34:03.636 --> 00:34:06.472
We'll go next year Charlie, all of us will.


00:34:07.873 --> 00:34:09.976
Yeah, yeah I'd like that.


00:34:14.880 --> 00:34:17.683
So how the hell d'you know
what a dog biscuit tastes like?


00:34:17.783 --> 00:34:19.852
- You never tried one?
- No, I'm not a dog.


00:34:19.954 --> 00:34:23.755
Well you have now 'cause,
these are dog biscuits.


00:34:29.728 --> 00:34:34.199
- Bill, what d'you think?
- I think this won't clear itself. Come on.


00:34:36.600 --> 00:34:38.103
Cheer up, nearly on our way home.


00:34:47.744 --> 00:34:48.813
Enter.


00:34:54.085 --> 00:34:55.552
Bill.


00:34:56.120 --> 00:34:57.989
The only news I want is good news.


00:34:58.089 --> 00:34:59.889
I believe we've reached the location sir.


00:35:00.724 --> 00:35:02.525
Directly beneath the German maxim.


00:35:04.827 --> 00:35:05.861
Uh well done.


00:35:07.697 --> 00:35:10.499
We'll conceal the detonation with
one of the mortar attacks.


00:35:10.599 --> 00:35:13.069
- HQ's getting me the schedule as we speak.
- Aye sir.


00:35:14.904 --> 00:35:17.140
Sir is there anyway
to double-check the coordinates?


00:35:17.974 --> 00:35:19.608
We don't wanna miss our only chance.


00:35:20.210 --> 00:35:22.178
Of course. I'll get someone
on to it right now.


00:35:23.811 --> 00:35:24.679
Alright.


00:35:35.258 --> 00:35:39.761
Baker, Marshall, I've got a job
for you two. No man's land, tonight.


00:35:46.834 --> 00:35:48.568
Easy. Easy.


00:35:48.668 --> 00:35:51.772
Will you shut the hell up,
how many times have I done this?


00:35:53.274 --> 00:35:55.876
Hey Woodsy, can you smell something?


00:35:55.977 --> 00:35:57.611
Oh, bloody sewers.


00:36:01.181 --> 00:36:02.681
I'm getting sick of the attitude.


00:36:03.817 --> 00:36:05.053
Don't get it.


00:36:08.155 --> 00:36:09.588
Put yourself in their boots.


00:36:10.991 --> 00:36:11.992
They don't know who we are.


00:36:15.395 --> 00:36:18.065
- Let me tell you a story about Private King.
- No, let's not.


00:36:20.366 --> 00:36:21.233
Huwww!


00:36:25.038 --> 00:36:27.273
Oh you cheeky bastard.


00:36:29.008 --> 00:36:30.342
Private King yeah.


00:36:30.443 --> 00:36:34.579
Hey. Private King. He's a 19-year-old lad.


00:36:35.147 --> 00:36:39.084
New to the front.
Part of a troop moving between trenches.


00:36:40.751 --> 00:36:43.788
And they were out for hours marching, full pack.


00:36:43.889 --> 00:36:48.293
Suddenly, King needs to take a crap,
right proper desperate, yeah?


00:36:49.260 --> 00:36:51.896
So he says to his CO.
The CO is like, "Yeah, fine,


00:36:52.297 --> 00:36:56.600
just catch us up after."
He goes off, does his business.


00:36:58.168 --> 00:37:00.671
Night's creeping in. He's in the forest.


00:37:00.771 --> 00:37:02.040
Sets off after his troop.


00:37:03.673 --> 00:37:04.942
Wrong bloody direction.


00:37:06.742 --> 00:37:07.643
In the morning..


00:37:09.212 --> 00:37:11.348
...soldiers pick him up, arrest him.


00:37:11.448 --> 00:37:12.648
For desertion?


00:37:13.217 --> 00:37:14.151
Aye.


00:37:15.952 --> 00:37:19.123
He protests his innocence.
"I was having a crap.


00:37:19.223 --> 00:37:20.958
I was having a crap, ask my CO."


00:37:21.756 --> 00:37:22.824
Only problem is..


00:37:24.093 --> 00:37:27.929
...CO's dead, isn't he?
German sniper clocked him an hour before.


00:37:29.398 --> 00:37:34.768
So with no one to vouch for his story,
court martial instantly returned a guilty verdict.


00:37:35.470 --> 00:37:40.741
And then it's a,
blindfold, bullet, unmarked grave. Gone.


00:37:41.209 --> 00:37:44.179
Christ that's no way to be remembered,
for everyone to think you're a coward.


00:37:44.279 --> 00:37:48.716
No. May as well just walk out into No Man's Land
and have the Boche do it for you.


00:37:49.951 --> 00:37:52.987
At least then you get called an hero.
Get a medal.


00:37:54.421 --> 00:37:59.094
Hey. So if them regular tommies
want to hate us, I say fine.


00:37:59.460 --> 00:38:02.296
Because on one side
they got maxim guns pointed at them.


00:38:02.396 --> 00:38:06.230
On the other, mad bastards
who would rather execute a kid then,


00:38:06.230 --> 00:38:08.435
believe he needed to take a shit.


00:38:14.474 --> 00:38:15.976
How many medals do you think we'll get?


00:38:17.111 --> 00:38:18.877
They don't give medals for likes of us.


00:38:18.978 --> 00:38:20.879
No. They give them to general's runners,


00:38:20.980 --> 00:38:23.283
ass lickers. Them folk.


00:38:23.383 --> 00:38:24.918
You're all having me on aren't you?


00:38:26.219 --> 00:38:29.688
It's like back home,
the bottom people, do all the work.


00:38:29.788 --> 00:38:33.258
Top brass take all the credit and then...
Well, when it goes right.


00:38:33.358 --> 00:38:36.761
- What if it goes wrong?
- It's a two way street lad.


00:38:36.861 --> 00:38:38.430
Praise goes up, shit comes down.


00:38:38.530 --> 00:38:40.465
That's just the way of life.


00:38:40.566 --> 00:38:42.467
Y'know, if all you can do is your best.


00:38:43.401 --> 00:38:44.802
That's all you can do.


00:38:46.305 --> 00:38:49.007
You're a poet you know that?


00:38:49.107 --> 00:38:52.343
- Bill. Those coordinates correct?
- Aye. Hellfire sent two chaps


00:38:52.443 --> 00:38:55.247
out into no man's land,
and they came back correct.


00:38:55.347 --> 00:38:56.948
Jolly good Harker.


00:38:57.915 --> 00:39:00.284
The mortar attack's scheduled
from 7:20 until 7:30,


00:39:00.384 --> 00:39:02.786
- should give you plenty of time.
- Plenty sir.


00:39:02.887 --> 00:39:05.755
Excellent. Excellent.


00:39:05.889 --> 00:39:08.291
Bill you do realize
what you're about to do don't you?


00:39:09.926 --> 00:39:11.760
Well we'll let you know when we've done it, sir.


00:39:11.861 --> 00:39:15.699
Good show. Good show.


00:39:18.535 --> 00:39:19.436
Alright.


00:39:58.838 --> 00:40:00.074
The bloody hell's that noise?


00:40:00.976 --> 00:40:05.078
Been living under a rock?
Poor sod got sent on some suicide mission,


00:40:05.178 --> 00:40:06.513
looking for machine gun posts.


00:40:07.414 --> 00:40:09.550
He's been stuck out there
for nearly two days now.


00:40:09.651 --> 00:40:11.051
I thought they came back.


00:40:11.151 --> 00:40:12.152
One of them did.


00:40:12.886 --> 00:40:13.987
Morning chaps.


00:40:16.490 --> 00:40:18.925
- Where's Bill?
- What are you doing?


00:40:19.859 --> 00:40:21.028
What does it look like?


00:40:23.195 --> 00:40:25.331
Don't be so bloody stupid, man.


00:40:25.431 --> 00:40:27.099
Alright Private Stockford,
you're up.


00:40:27.867 --> 00:40:29.801
- Well come on!
- Yes sir sir!


00:40:53.992 --> 00:40:56.428
If you go up there you are a dead man!


00:40:56.528 --> 00:40:58.271
Do you understand?


00:40:59.571 --> 00:41:01.265
This is madness.


00:41:01.265 --> 00:41:02.333
Wait!


00:41:22.585 --> 00:41:24.455
Help me, please.


00:41:25.089 --> 00:41:27.457
Alright lad, we're gonna get you down.


00:42:12.099 --> 00:42:14.568
Watch out then. All right, all right.


00:42:16.736 --> 00:42:19.406
You should get yourself checked
for insanity, old boy.


00:42:20.441 --> 00:42:23.443
- That's just for the COs, mate.
- Brother!


00:42:25.745 --> 00:42:27.680
Following this morning's mission..


00:42:29.047 --> 00:42:35.421
...HQ has deemed it necessary
for the.. mining effort, to expand.


00:42:36.522 --> 00:42:41.360
We will continue
on to the Messines as, as planned.


00:42:43.328 --> 00:42:44.263
Jolly good news sir.


00:42:47.031 --> 00:42:48.032
Quite.


00:42:49.601 --> 00:42:50.702
You wanted me sir.


00:42:52.571 --> 00:42:54.071
Yes Hawkins just a moment.


00:42:56.340 --> 00:42:57.208
Well then.


00:43:02.213 --> 00:43:03.114
Carry on Jack.


00:43:06.650 --> 00:43:07.685
Harker.


00:43:21.364 --> 00:43:23.533
So we're expanding the tunnels
to the Messines ridge?


00:43:25.134 --> 00:43:27.137
That's right.
No concern of yours anymore.


00:43:27.537 --> 00:43:29.172
Well the ridge is over a thousand feet away.


00:43:30.107 --> 00:43:32.575
Thanks to you and your men
we have the know-how to get it done.


00:43:32.675 --> 00:43:34.577
There's new mining teams
being trained back home.


00:43:35.211 --> 00:43:36.480
With what experience?


00:43:37.613 --> 00:43:40.583
Sending the wrong men down there
without the right skills would be irresponsible.


00:43:40.683 --> 00:43:42.618
Irresponsible, is it?


00:43:43.751 --> 00:43:46.822
What the bloody hell do you call
your performance out there this morning?


00:43:46.923 --> 00:43:50.492
Saving a man's life.
What a soldier's supposed to do.


00:43:50.592 --> 00:43:52.660
Soldiers follow direct orders given to them,


00:43:52.760 --> 00:43:54.496
they don't saunter into no man's land


00:43:54.597 --> 00:43:55.730
in the hope of being labelled a hero.


00:43:55.830 --> 00:43:57.565
The boy was out there because of us,


00:43:58.166 --> 00:44:00.261
checking our coordinates.
What would you have me do?


00:44:00.261 --> 00:44:02.402
Men die every day, doing what we tell them.


00:44:02.503 --> 00:44:05.440
It's not pretty, it's necessary.


00:44:06.374 --> 00:44:10.077
They run into no man's land,
they fight, and they die, for each other,


00:44:10.177 --> 00:44:12.312
not for a slap on the back
or a medal on the chest.


00:44:15.382 --> 00:44:17.284
Perhaps it's a good job you're leaving.


00:44:27.493 --> 00:44:29.061
You've done your bit bill.


00:44:29.863 --> 00:44:31.030
It's time to go home.


00:44:32.198 --> 00:44:33.766
I'll put a word in for you and your men.


00:44:38.638 --> 00:44:40.105
We checked the tunnel.


00:44:40.205 --> 00:44:42.542
There's some faint sounds scraping.


00:44:43.643 --> 00:44:45.478
It looks like the Germans
are digging now, too.


00:44:59.857 --> 00:45:03.361
- Harry where's your bag?
- Didn't see point in bringing it.


00:45:04.295 --> 00:45:06.230
Logistics are saying the trains
might be held up.


00:45:06.330 --> 00:45:08.732
There's, some commotion with the Froggies,


00:45:08.832 --> 00:45:10.701
taking on, the ones meant for us.


00:45:11.535 --> 00:45:14.371
Oh well, have to entertain ourselves then, yeah?


00:45:24.380 --> 00:45:26.115
Three, bloody hours.


00:45:28.585 --> 00:45:30.553
Calm down Charlie. It'll turn up.


00:45:38.361 --> 00:45:39.863
I've known you for 20 years Bill.


00:45:41.164 --> 00:45:43.198
And I can read you like an half-penny Marvel.


00:45:44.199 --> 00:45:46.635
- And?
- I know when you're gonna say it's time to dig


00:45:46.735 --> 00:45:50.372
and when it's time for a brew, but I also know
when you're gonna say, job's not done yet.


00:45:50.472 --> 00:45:53.575
- Well the Job's not done.
- Whoa. Hellfire said we're done.


00:45:54.242 --> 00:45:56.477
- Said we did our bit.
- I know Shorty.


00:45:57.479 --> 00:45:59.381
Without us those tunnels are gonna fail.


00:46:00.382 --> 00:46:01.582
Without the tunnels there's no bomb,


00:46:01.682 --> 00:46:03.651
no bomb means years more
of the same shit


00:46:03.751 --> 00:46:05.252
and thousands more men dying.


00:46:05.786 --> 00:46:07.889
- Maybe even us losing the war.
- We don't know that.


00:46:07.990 --> 00:46:10.157
Yeah. Yeah we do lad.


00:46:12.326 --> 00:46:14.260
It's a good job
I didn't bring my kit, eh Bill?


00:46:15.595 --> 00:46:17.298
Wait Harry? Where're you going?


00:46:19.366 --> 00:46:20.300
Bloody hell.


00:46:21.469 --> 00:46:24.638
Hellfire said they got
whole new team of miners down there now.


00:46:25.538 --> 00:46:26.773
Showed them how to cut the clay.


00:46:27.807 --> 00:46:29.776
And you trust them to get
the job done do you?


00:46:30.710 --> 00:46:34.246
If your life, your family's life depended on it,


00:46:34.949 --> 00:46:36.383
you trust them to get it done?


00:46:37.517 --> 00:46:38.651
I don't think I can.


00:46:40.386 --> 00:46:42.354
- What's going on?
- Bill's gone mad.


00:46:43.288 --> 00:46:44.657
Harry's gone back to the front.


00:46:46.392 --> 00:46:48.460
You just trying to prove
sommit to these people?


00:46:49.495 --> 00:46:50.595
That Fielding?


00:46:53.231 --> 00:46:55.869
Sod Fielding. Sod Haig.


00:46:57.402 --> 00:46:59.537
This is about all the men
they don't care about.


00:47:00.605 --> 00:47:01.673
The ones like us.


00:47:03.041 --> 00:47:05.777
I hope to God no one ever has
to see a place like this again.


00:47:06.711 --> 00:47:08.846
But to do that the job's gotta be finished,


00:47:08.947 --> 00:47:11.248
and I believe we're the only ones can do it.


00:47:12.850 --> 00:47:13.851
Shorty?


00:47:20.925 --> 00:47:23.560
- Oh Jesus Christ.
- You're not really thinkin' it.


00:47:24.929 --> 00:47:26.730
Bill, Bill, I-I wanna go home.


00:47:26.830 --> 00:47:30.199
- I just, want to go home.
- Then go home Charlie.


00:47:30.299 --> 00:47:31.401
You don't owe anyone anything.


00:47:32.402 --> 00:47:33.071
None of you do.


00:47:34.804 --> 00:47:35.972
- What if we did stay?
- George!


00:47:36.073 --> 00:47:36.940
I'm just sayin'.


00:47:38.008 --> 00:47:40.276
It's gonna take six months to dig that tunnel.


00:47:40.810 --> 00:47:42.378
- The Germans know we're coming.
- Aye.


00:47:44.547 --> 00:47:46.682
Aye. I know, George.


00:47:49.517 --> 00:47:52.889
No, no no this is daft.
We-we're here. We-we're goin' home.


00:47:54.723 --> 00:47:56.591
If the bloody train ever sodding shows up.


00:48:00.795 --> 00:48:01.997
You know what I'm gonna say.


00:48:03.665 --> 00:48:04.699
You've gotta be joking.


00:48:06.600 --> 00:48:07.568
We're not stayin'.


00:48:10.505 --> 00:48:11.406
George please.


00:48:13.741 --> 00:48:14.909
You don't have to come back.


00:48:17.344 --> 00:48:18.512
I'm sure they'd understand.


00:48:29.423 --> 00:48:30.590
See you Charlie.


00:48:35.963 --> 00:48:36.896
I'm not stayin'.


00:48:38.498 --> 00:48:39.599
Bunch of idiots.


00:49:02.020 --> 00:49:03.387
<i>My darling Jane.</i>


00:49:04.990 --> 00:49:07.425
<i>I know each month I say I'm closer to home.</i>


00:49:08.659 --> 00:49:10.494
<i>But war makes us break promises.</i>


00:49:11.729 --> 00:49:14.032
<i>And the truth is, I'm even farther from it.</i>


00:49:16.001 --> 00:49:18.736
<i>These past few months, time has ground by.</i>


00:49:19.503 --> 00:49:22.343
Messines Trench, March 1917. Four months later.


00:49:19.503 --> 00:49:22.039
<i>Our new tunnels inch closer to the German lines,</i>


00:49:22.705 --> 00:49:24.508
<i>to the biggest explosion in history.</i>


00:49:25.509 --> 00:49:27.677
<i>And I know it's only us can make it happen.</i>


00:49:29.679 --> 00:49:30.981
<i>The work is slow.</i>


00:49:32.115 --> 00:49:36.519
<i>We constantly listen out for the German tunnels,
and pray they don't find us.</i>


00:49:39.688 --> 00:49:41.523
<i>They say when a soldier dies,</i>


00:49:41.958 --> 00:49:44.929
<i>he becomes a patriot.
As the war goes on,</i>


00:49:45.528 --> 00:49:47.596
<i>it seems I know more and more patriots.</i>


00:49:49.665 --> 00:49:52.400
- Anything?
- Guess I must be hearing...


00:50:12.520 --> 00:50:13.521
Excuse me Madam.


00:50:14.490 --> 00:50:18.758
I'm afraid I have some rather,
bad news to deliver. Your husband.


00:50:20.794 --> 00:50:22.998
Do you need a chair? I-I can go inside.


00:50:24.431 --> 00:50:25.398
Mrs. Brown?


00:50:26.100 --> 00:50:28.870
- No.
- No you don't want a chair?


00:50:28.970 --> 00:50:31.038
No, I-I'm not Mrs. Brown.


00:50:31.671 --> 00:50:34.708
I'm Mrs. Hawkin.
Sarah Brown lives at number four.


00:50:37.143 --> 00:50:40.714
Oh, my word I'm.. I'm ever so sorry, ehh...


00:50:42.148 --> 00:50:46.418
Let me just um, yes it-it says 14.


00:50:47.486 --> 00:50:48.921
I am I am so so sorry.


00:50:49.021 --> 00:50:51.423
Um... thank you for your time.


00:50:52.225 --> 00:50:53.093
Sorry.


00:51:23.221 --> 00:51:26.522
Field Marshal Haig in his infinite wisdom
has given us a date.


00:51:28.825 --> 00:51:31.662
- Seventh of June, it's three months from now.
- Three months?


00:51:32.262 --> 00:51:35.464
But with the way things are going,
we're not even getting through half our usual distance.


00:51:35.564 --> 00:51:38.135
- It's non-negotiable, I'm afraid.
- It's too crowded down there.


00:51:38.902 --> 00:51:41.437
Since the Germans joined in the fun,
we've had a team running into them


00:51:41.537 --> 00:51:42.838
near enough every bloody day.


00:51:43.240 --> 00:51:45.007
We're spending more time
dodging them than we are


00:51:45.107 --> 00:51:46.609
actually moving forward.


00:51:49.712 --> 00:51:50.578
Alright.


00:51:52.181 --> 00:51:53.115
So we go deeper.


00:51:54.516 --> 00:51:57.019
Below the blue clay line
where the Boche won't even think to follow.


00:51:57.119 --> 00:51:58.753
We can't do it, sir.


00:51:58.854 --> 00:52:02.224
Our current location is here.
Messines here.


00:52:03.224 --> 00:52:07.629
Now if we dig deeper that'll take us to here,
that's 300-foot extra ground to cover.


00:52:08.164 --> 00:52:10.999
- There's just not enough time.
- Yes but staying here is suicide.


00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:14.035
Sooner or later every team
runs into a German gallery.


00:52:14.136 --> 00:52:16.503
I've lost eight in the past week
I don't want to lose a ninth.


00:52:16.603 --> 00:52:17.538
Neither do I.


00:52:18.907 --> 00:52:21.242
But if we work any harder
they'll be nothing left of us to lose.


00:52:24.179 --> 00:52:26.915
Only thing we can do is, stay the course


00:52:27.015 --> 00:52:28.148
and hope we get lucky.


00:52:29.016 --> 00:52:31.718
Luck's not something I like
to hang my hat on, old boy.


00:52:42.795 --> 00:52:43.796
Here take this.


00:52:47.233 --> 00:52:48.101
Just in case.


00:52:58.643 --> 00:53:01.046
Bill. If this is successful..


00:53:02.181 --> 00:53:05.550
...could change the face of the war,
no more stalemates no more trenches,


00:53:06.018 --> 00:53:07.085
we march to Berlin.


00:53:08.153 --> 00:53:09.653
You could be the man to achieve that.


00:53:18.795 --> 00:53:20.132
You right Charlie?


00:53:21.665 --> 00:53:23.534
Yeah not heard from Maggie
for a couple of weeks.


00:53:24.601 --> 00:53:26.303
Just.. gettin' a bit worried about her.


00:53:31.142 --> 00:53:33.710
I'm sure she's fine. Busy is all.


00:53:34.178 --> 00:53:36.047
She runs the plant as much as Rogers does.


00:53:37.113 --> 00:53:38.747
Yeah, guess so.


00:53:42.786 --> 00:53:43.786
Funny though, innit it?


00:53:45.188 --> 00:53:46.089
What is?


00:53:47.390 --> 00:53:48.893
Well, when you're at home...


00:53:50.260 --> 00:53:52.929
...getting a letter,
it don't mean nothin' really.


00:53:53.029 --> 00:53:54.064
But out here.


00:53:56.198 --> 00:53:57.232
Did y'know.


00:53:59.369 --> 00:54:03.671
Next time I see the postman on Applegate Street I'm..
gonna want shake his hand.


00:54:04.672 --> 00:54:05.673
I really am.


00:54:09.144 --> 00:54:11.346
You think I'm being stupid about it don't ya?


00:54:11.447 --> 00:54:12.647
No.


00:54:15.083 --> 00:54:15.983
No of course not.


00:54:19.421 --> 00:54:20.787
I think I really love her.


00:54:26.261 --> 00:54:27.727
Another day in the sun gents.


00:56:23.171 --> 00:56:24.105
Get the stuff.


00:56:41.889 --> 00:56:42.789
Move!


00:56:48.162 --> 00:56:50.930
As much as I hate to say it, you were right.


00:56:51.030 --> 00:56:54.467
I'll get that in writing, shall I?
How much deeper do you think you need to go?


00:56:54.567 --> 00:56:57.370
Well if we're going to get under 'em,
it will need to be over 100 feet.


00:56:58.004 --> 00:57:00.772
- But with that there's gonna be new problems.
- Such as?


00:57:00.873 --> 00:57:03.909
The deeper down we go, the more
the composition of the ground will change.


00:57:04.910 --> 00:57:08.314
Also we're below sea level.
And then there's all the stuff I can't predict.


00:57:08.948 --> 00:57:11.383
Cave-ins. Oxygen drop outs.


00:57:11.483 --> 00:57:14.186
And we'll need canaries in case of gas pockets.


00:57:14.453 --> 00:57:16.288
Can you do it in time?


00:57:16.923 --> 00:57:21.827
I don't know. We're the only crew that can,
we're working every hour God sends.


00:57:21.926 --> 00:57:23.527
We could do with Him sending us a few more.


00:57:23.628 --> 00:57:26.064
Well focus all your energies on a single tunnel.


00:57:26.164 --> 00:57:29.467
Increase shift times. You have to do it
just with less shut-eye.


00:57:53.323 --> 00:57:57.227
Right lads up we get.
Beauty sleep's wasted on the ugly.


00:57:57.327 --> 00:57:59.428
Bloody hell Bill
we've only just got us heads down.


00:58:00.562 --> 00:58:04.267
- We're here to do a job.
- I never wanted to sodding be here in the first place.


00:58:07.903 --> 00:58:08.570
Listen Bill.


00:58:10.372 --> 00:58:12.374
They've been working solid they need a rest.


00:58:12.474 --> 00:58:15.144
- And so do you.
- And we can have as long as we want when job's done.


00:58:16.045 --> 00:58:19.213
- Only a couple more weeks.
- Look at 'em.


00:58:19.314 --> 00:58:24.320
Look. They're on the verge of collapsing.
You'd never do this back at home.


00:58:24.419 --> 00:58:25.553
We're not at home are we?


00:58:27.221 --> 00:58:28.456
Like Hellfire says,


00:58:29.057 --> 00:58:31.292
"We do this, and the war's over."


00:58:34.629 --> 00:58:37.364
Come on. Five minutes and we're at the face.


00:58:59.486 --> 00:59:01.221
One more bag, nearly there.


00:59:06.125 --> 00:59:07.393
Did anyone feel sommit?


00:59:07.493 --> 00:59:08.861
Shh-shh-shh-shh-shh.


00:59:09.995 --> 00:59:11.130
I thought I heard a crack.


00:59:35.252 --> 00:59:36.320
You all right?


00:59:39.324 --> 00:59:40.357
George no!


00:59:51.368 --> 00:59:53.536
Medic! Medic!


01:00:02.745 --> 01:00:04.147
Bastard!


01:00:04.247 --> 01:00:06.349
You'll bloody kill us I warned ya!


01:00:06.449 --> 01:00:08.251
Get off me! Get off me!


01:00:10.086 --> 01:00:11.520
They will bloody shoot you.


01:00:13.422 --> 01:00:16.626
You see, this is what you get,


01:00:16.726 --> 01:00:20.061
when you let common sewer workers
play at being soldiers.


01:00:20.162 --> 01:00:22.164
Nothing to be concerned about sir
they're just overworked.


01:00:22.264 --> 01:00:23.597
Oh we're all overworked.


01:00:24.633 --> 01:00:27.469
A lack of discipline
is a lack of discipline.


01:00:28.570 --> 01:00:30.638
No ifs, no buts.


01:00:31.572 --> 01:00:33.307
I'm a busy man, Jack.


01:00:34.877 --> 01:00:40.314
So you and your underground trolls here
can apologize for wasting my time.


01:00:41.182 --> 01:00:43.017
This troll's name is Private Stockford.


01:00:43.117 --> 01:00:45.252
And with all due respect, sir,


01:00:45.352 --> 01:00:48.721
you can shove your little stick
up your plumy little ass.


01:00:48.823 --> 01:00:51.291
- Get off!
- Sergeant!


01:00:54.661 --> 01:00:59.632
Take him and him,
for field punishment number one.


01:00:59.732 --> 01:01:02.735
- Insubordination.
- Sir! You!


01:01:02.837 --> 01:01:05.071
Get up on your feet. Get on your feet.


01:01:06.139 --> 01:01:08.240
Get over there. You, face that way.


01:01:08.340 --> 01:01:10.509
Face that way.
Stand to attention. Stand next to him.


01:01:11.578 --> 01:01:13.312
Double [...] quick march!


01:01:13.412 --> 01:01:15.380
Hurry up, hike up, hike up,
hike up, hike up,


01:01:15.481 --> 01:01:17.349
hike up, hike up,
hike up, hike up.


01:01:17.449 --> 01:01:22.321
Left, right, left, right, left, right,
left, right, left, right, left.


01:01:25.424 --> 01:01:27.725
Detail! Halt!


01:01:31.263 --> 01:01:35.666
Hawkin. On that door facing me, go.
Stockford, by that door facing me, go.


01:01:36.835 --> 01:01:39.336
- Turn around. Private. Tie him up.
- S'arnt.


01:01:42.640 --> 01:01:44.408
Hawkin hands out in front of me.


01:01:46.109 --> 01:01:48.078
- Make sure it's tight, boy.
- S'arnt.


01:01:50.747 --> 01:01:52.215
- Ready?
- S'arnt.


01:01:52.850 --> 01:01:54.050
Raise!


01:02:01.324 --> 01:02:02.526
- Fall back.
- S'arnt.


01:02:04.627 --> 01:02:07.062
Detail. About turn.


01:02:08.498 --> 01:02:14.203
Quick march, hurry up, right, yah.
We'll be back, in the morning.


01:02:23.578 --> 01:02:25.246
That pompous prat wit' his stick.


01:02:26.148 --> 01:02:28.550
Is that the type of man
we're supposed get respect from here?


01:02:28.650 --> 01:02:31.185
- Oh give it a bloody rest will ya?
- I'm being serious.


01:02:31.753 --> 01:02:34.922
When I'm 100 feet underground trying
me best not to be burnt alive or crushed,


01:02:34.922 --> 01:02:37.525
- I just want to know what it's all for.
- We don't work for him do we?


01:02:37.625 --> 01:02:40.261
- We work for Hellfire.
- I don't work for him.


01:02:40.361 --> 01:02:44.364
I don't trust him, I bloody well
work for you, and I did trust you.


01:02:44.464 --> 01:02:45.834
When have I ever lied to you?


01:02:45.935 --> 01:02:47.467
You're lyin' to yourself now.


01:02:48.269 --> 01:02:51.271
That great victory you're waitin' for,
not gonna happen.


01:02:51.806 --> 01:02:54.674
This war's just going to trundle
along no matter what we do,


01:02:54.774 --> 01:02:58.211
and the only reason you're here is so that
when people ask what happened back at home,


01:02:58.312 --> 01:03:00.847
- you can hold your bloody head high.
- That's bollocks that.


01:03:00.948 --> 01:03:02.748
Is it? Is it?


01:03:04.017 --> 01:03:07.653
I've lived long enough to know
that the only person that can really judge you,


01:03:07.753 --> 01:03:10.189
is the one that's in your own bloody boots Bill.


01:03:15.561 --> 01:03:19.531
All I'm saying is that,
y'know those that know you they respect you.


01:03:19.631 --> 01:03:24.337
They know what you put on line.
I'm talking about, Peter and Jane.


01:03:27.205 --> 01:03:28.239
And me.


01:03:29.441 --> 01:03:32.577
Sometimes. When you're not being
a bloody pigheaded moron.


01:03:58.735 --> 01:04:00.203
Hurts doesn't it, Hawkin?


01:04:01.405 --> 01:04:02.405
Yes sir.


01:04:03.339 --> 01:04:04.707
The army doesn't tolerate insubordination,


01:04:05.375 --> 01:04:06.844
under any circumstances.


01:04:08.610 --> 01:04:12.348
I however, admire a man
who stands for what he believes in.


01:04:12.850 --> 01:04:16.351
Who doesn't leave a man
in the field to die, alone.


01:04:37.672 --> 01:04:39.341
You breathe a word of this to anybody


01:04:39.441 --> 01:04:40.942
and I'll have your guts for garters.


01:04:41.742 --> 01:04:43.945
And you'll be on latrine duty for a month.


01:04:45.513 --> 01:04:46.613
Yes s'arnt.


01:05:05.932 --> 01:05:09.302
- Hellfire say what he wants s'arnt?
- You'll see, soon enough.


01:05:10.970 --> 01:05:12.304
Think that'll work on the Germans?


01:05:12.404 --> 01:05:14.707
Not a chance. We've run out of sausage.


01:05:16.643 --> 01:05:17.676
Uh-huh.


01:05:20.646 --> 01:05:21.580
Sir.


01:05:22.614 --> 01:05:24.515
Ah. Thank you s'arnt. Carry on.


01:05:26.485 --> 01:05:27.453
All right chaps.


01:05:28.021 --> 01:05:29.888
Bit of R&R, before the final push.


01:05:29.988 --> 01:05:31.957
Haven't got the time for a, week in Bognor


01:05:32.057 --> 01:05:34.726
so uh, this will have to suffice.


01:05:34.827 --> 01:05:36.494
I think we're more the football type sir.


01:05:36.594 --> 01:05:37.695
Here.


01:05:38.730 --> 01:05:41.265
- W.G. Grace gave me that.
- W.G. who?


01:05:42.766 --> 01:05:45.570
- Greatest cricketer of all time.
- That good thing is it?


01:05:45.670 --> 01:05:47.940
Yes it is. You, wicket.


01:05:49.006 --> 01:05:50.842
Harold no smoking on the field of play.


01:05:52.944 --> 01:05:54.846
Alright just stand there, and catch it.


01:05:55.712 --> 01:05:58.615
Hawkin go long, George in.
Right, who wants to bowl?


01:05:58.715 --> 01:06:00.817
- What?
- He's asking who wants to lob a ball at CO.


01:06:01.650 --> 01:06:03.553
No, no!


01:06:06.057 --> 01:06:07.790
- I didn't mean it!
- Mail for Private MacDonald.


01:06:07.891 --> 01:06:09.358
- Which one?
- C.


01:06:09.458 --> 01:06:11.327
It's about damn time she wrote to me.


01:06:12.062 --> 01:06:15.297
Alright, George. You're in bat.
Try and use the right end.


01:06:16.699 --> 01:06:20.335
- Send it son, go on.
- Legs together George legs together.


01:06:23.005 --> 01:06:24.373
Ohhhhhh!


01:06:25.908 --> 01:06:28.811
That's it. Get it bowler,
get him out come on, get him out!


01:06:28.911 --> 01:06:32.915
Oh hahahahaha, well done.


01:06:33.015 --> 01:06:35.851
- Well that's it then, that's a quick game this cricket...
- Charlie!


01:06:37.786 --> 01:06:40.654
Charlie! Hey, Charlie!


01:06:44.758 --> 01:06:45.592
Charlie!


01:06:48.897 --> 01:06:50.532
Charlie! Hey!


01:06:56.370 --> 01:06:57.537
Charlie!


01:06:58.906 --> 01:07:01.341
- Charlie! no! Charlie!
- Out of my way! Out of my way!


01:07:01.441 --> 01:07:02.544
What the bloody hell are you doing man,


01:07:02.544 --> 01:07:04.477
get down! Get down!


01:07:05.678 --> 01:07:07.480
- Jesus Christ.
- No!


01:07:07.948 --> 01:07:09.315
Charlie! Charlie!


01:07:09.817 --> 01:07:12.052
No! No Charlie! Charlie!


01:07:31.871 --> 01:07:32.872
Charlie!


01:07:33.840 --> 01:07:35.106
No! Charlie!


01:07:59.729 --> 01:08:00.663
Oh Lord.


01:08:23.619 --> 01:08:24.753
<i>My dearest Jane.</i>


01:08:26.222 --> 01:08:28.757
<i>I'm writing to you
with the heaviest of hearts.</i>


01:08:31.492 --> 01:08:33.761
<i>Last night our Charlie took his own life.</i>


01:08:35.131 --> 01:08:37.465
<i>Harold had warned me that
the men were close to breaking,</i>


01:08:37.565 --> 01:08:40.635
<i>but I wouldn't see it. I should have seen it.</i>


01:08:41.937 --> 01:08:44.172
<i>He had just received a letter
from Margaret Parish.</i>


01:08:45.173 --> 01:08:47.042
<i>It seems Ned had finally come home,</i>


01:08:47.142 --> 01:08:49.044
<i>and so she had called off their love affair.</i>


01:08:50.543 --> 01:08:52.779
<i>It's heartbreaking, what love can do,</i>


01:08:52.880 --> 01:08:55.616
<i>more powerful than anything
over here I could honestly say.</i>


01:08:56.549 --> 01:08:58.986
<i>Would you tell Charlie's mother
he died honourably?</i>


01:08:59.086 --> 01:09:01.956
<i>It would be much better coming
from you than a stranger in uniform.</i>


01:09:02.656 --> 01:09:03.791
<i>It's the least he deserves.</i>


01:09:05.993 --> 01:09:08.661
Oh no, no.


01:09:08.761 --> 01:09:10.163
- I'm so sorry.
- No!


01:09:10.263 --> 01:09:11.197
I'm so sorry.


01:09:12.099 --> 01:09:13.767
<i>Despite what has happened,</i>


01:09:13.868 --> 01:09:15.068
<i>the team is still working without rest.</i>


01:09:16.236 --> 01:09:19.406
<i>George is showing more strength
than I can imagine to carry on.</i>


01:09:20.273 --> 01:09:23.509
<i>We are near our end but...
mad as it seems,</i>


01:09:24.510 --> 01:09:26.112
<i>I'm not sure if I want it to stop.</i>


01:09:26.212 --> 01:09:29.447
<i>Because if I do, I don't know who I'll be.</i>


01:09:30.015 --> 01:09:35.120
<i>Part of me wants all this blood and terror,
because I know I can be of some worth in stopping it.</i>


01:09:36.155 --> 01:09:39.656
<i>And without it,
I'm just another man in a flat cap.</i>


01:09:40.793 --> 01:09:45.064
<i>But part of me knows my greatest achievement
lies at home with you and the life we had made.</i>


01:09:46.831 --> 01:09:48.199
<i>Maybe you were right all along.</i>


01:09:49.133 --> 01:09:50.535
<i>I'm just a bloody fool.</i>


01:09:51.136 --> 01:09:53.237
<i>All my love is with you and Peter.</i>


01:09:54.005 --> 01:09:56.573
<i>Yours forever. William.</i>


01:10:08.251 --> 01:10:13.153
June 6, 1917. Eve of the attack.


01:10:15.658 --> 01:10:17.159
Weren't able to do an oxygen test.


01:10:18.228 --> 01:10:19.830
So we'll just have to go for it.


01:10:20.663 --> 01:10:22.565
That's all right, lads. I've got it sorted.


01:10:29.172 --> 01:10:31.974
- What's that?
- Apparently army's run out of canaries


01:10:32.074 --> 01:10:35.710
so I've had to improvise.
Say hello to Fielding Jr. here.


01:10:37.079 --> 01:10:39.949
- It looks dead.
- It's not dead, it's pissed.


01:10:40.648 --> 01:10:42.716
I gave tot of rum.
As long as we can see it breathing


01:10:42.817 --> 01:10:45.153
- it's all that matters.
- Fielding takes away our miners


01:10:45.253 --> 01:10:46.956
and we replace them with a pissed rat?


01:10:47.356 --> 01:10:48.555
Seems a fair swap.


01:10:50.258 --> 01:10:52.760
If you're quite
finished with the local wildlife.


01:10:54.129 --> 01:10:55.162
At ease, men.


01:10:57.799 --> 01:10:58.732
I'm very proud.


01:11:00.901 --> 01:11:02.602
Very proud of each and every one of you.


01:11:04.138 --> 01:11:05.006
Your belief.


01:11:06.374 --> 01:11:08.775
Your courage in the face
of great difficulty.


01:11:09.376 --> 01:11:11.744
You pretty much lived
your whole lives underground,


01:11:11.845 --> 01:11:13.678
out of sight, unrecognized.


01:11:14.782 --> 01:11:15.883
But tonight...


01:11:17.217 --> 01:11:18.584
...in a matter of hours...


01:11:19.919 --> 01:11:22.088
...thousands of our boys
will be torn to ribbons.


01:11:22.789 --> 01:11:23.891
Unless we set that bomb.


01:11:25.892 --> 01:11:28.061
This isn't about what
we can prove to the top brass.


01:11:30.063 --> 01:11:31.798
This is about what we can do for our men.


01:11:37.170 --> 01:11:38.137
Gentlemen...


01:11:39.637 --> 01:11:40.305
...tonight...


01:11:41.907 --> 01:11:43.076
...we may not make history...


01:11:45.310 --> 01:11:47.645
...but we'll certainly change
the bloody geography.


01:11:52.020 --> 01:11:53.222
George.


01:11:56.021 --> 01:11:57.022
Shorty.


01:11:59.857 --> 01:12:00.723
Harold.


01:12:09.731 --> 01:12:10.867
It's been a privilege.


01:12:11.668 --> 01:12:12.937
Thank you sir.


01:12:13.770 --> 01:12:15.005
I was wrong about you Bill.


01:12:16.005 --> 01:12:17.673
You're a fine soldier.


01:12:26.136 --> 01:12:29.835
03:00 AM.
Three hours before the attack.


01:12:41.396 --> 01:12:43.265
Hey. Time.


01:12:52.707 --> 01:12:54.876
Listen. They're close.


01:13:09.123 --> 01:13:10.191
It's Harold.


01:13:11.092 --> 01:13:12.993
Shorty I need you calm, right?


01:13:14.194 --> 01:13:15.061
Yeah.


01:13:17.398 --> 01:13:18.697
Bill we need more bags.


01:13:36.449 --> 01:13:37.850
Hey wait wait wait wait wait.


01:13:38.517 --> 01:13:40.986
Shorty you're imagining things,
snap out of it.


01:13:41.086 --> 01:13:41.921
Give me a sec.


01:13:57.302 --> 01:13:58.369
It's clear.


01:14:00.205 --> 01:14:01.172
George!


01:14:02.373 --> 01:14:04.163
Shhhhh...


01:14:06.978 --> 01:14:08.179
Pick yourself up lad.


01:14:19.156 --> 01:14:21.457
If we find a German tunnel
we've got to blow it, you know that.


01:14:21.557 --> 01:14:24.494
And what if one of their galleries
is next to the chamber?


01:14:24.595 --> 01:14:25.761
I need to see.


01:14:52.153 --> 01:14:53.054
Bill!


01:14:53.989 --> 01:14:55.490
Get your bloody arse back here.


01:15:07.401 --> 01:15:09.536
Seems to be heading a few degrees west.


01:15:09.637 --> 01:15:11.438
The chamber should be safe from the blast.


01:15:11.538 --> 01:15:13.374
Let's get the charges
and bring the whole thing down.


01:15:13.474 --> 01:15:14.775
- [German]
- Bill move shit!


01:15:48.341 --> 01:15:49.808
George!


01:16:25.208 --> 01:16:26.376
Get off me!


01:16:27.477 --> 01:16:28.845
What the bloody hell?


01:16:29.312 --> 01:16:31.614
- [...] the tunnel!
- Bill it's gone.


01:16:31.715 --> 01:16:33.349
It's gone, the whole thing came down.


01:16:35.385 --> 01:16:37.156
The chamber might still be intact,
let's get back to work.


01:16:37.156 --> 01:16:40.956
No no no it'll take hours to redig,
it's over Bill, forget it.


01:16:41.423 --> 01:16:43.125
The whole thing. Gone.


01:16:46.428 --> 01:16:47.596
Ohh the German tunnel.


01:16:50.998 --> 01:16:53.454
- Part of their tunnel runs right alongside ours.
- Whoa whoa whoa whoa.


01:16:53.454 --> 01:16:56.372
- No no no no! The chamber's collapsed!
- All we have to do is,


01:16:56.472 --> 01:17:00.108
find the right spot, break through,
we're right back there in the chamber!


01:17:00.208 --> 01:17:02.410
There are a load of bullets
that's going to disagree with that, Bill.


01:17:02.510 --> 01:17:05.880
The German procedure means they'll have
to scrap their tunnels, start a new one.


01:17:06.347 --> 01:17:08.883
- They'll expect us to do the same.
- No!


01:17:08.983 --> 01:17:10.884
It's a bloody suicide mission Bill,
you're own your own.


01:17:10.884 --> 01:17:13.287
- The time of attack's set in stone.
- No.


01:17:13.388 --> 01:17:16.890
At half past six our boys are going
to be charging straight to their deaths,


01:17:16.990 --> 01:17:18.258
unless we do this.


01:17:21.128 --> 01:17:21.996
No.


01:17:28.652 --> 01:17:29.535
Harry...


01:17:30.703 --> 01:17:35.608
...when you said I didn't have to come here
to prove myself, you were right.


01:17:37.543 --> 01:17:40.212
When you called me
a bloody pigheaded moron, you were right.


01:17:42.181 --> 01:17:45.217
Everyone of us is worth as much as any general.


01:17:45.317 --> 01:17:48.153
And I should have seen that years ago.
I'm sorry.


01:17:48.720 --> 01:17:51.424
But right now, we've got a simple choice to make.


01:17:53.292 --> 01:17:57.962
We either stay here do nothing give up,
because we think we might fail.


01:17:58.764 --> 01:18:01.566
Or we get back in there
and we do what we came here for.


01:18:02.500 --> 01:18:06.537
Not to be heroes, but because
it's the right thing to do.


01:18:10.508 --> 01:18:12.142
Let's get our bloody gear then eh?


01:18:15.212 --> 01:18:17.481
Georgie, you stay here.


01:18:18.348 --> 01:18:21.285
- I wrong to push you to do this.
- I'll be fine.


01:18:21.385 --> 01:18:23.353
Yeah you didn't look fine
when them Krauts jumped us.


01:18:23.454 --> 01:18:24.421
I'm sorry.


01:18:26.389 --> 01:18:27.457
I just couldn't.


01:18:28.292 --> 01:18:29.326
It won't happen again.


01:18:32.695 --> 01:18:33.996
We finish this together.


01:18:43.773 --> 01:18:45.474
At least someone's having a good time.


01:18:46.608 --> 01:18:50.710
05:00 AM. An hour before the attack.


01:19:39.325 --> 01:19:40.425
Shhhh.


01:19:58.210 --> 01:19:59.477
Ah!


01:20:04.516 --> 01:20:08.586
George, go back to breakthrough point
and stand lookout.


01:20:08.686 --> 01:20:10.254
Any activity let us know.


01:20:49.358 --> 01:20:50.259
Get the stuff.


01:21:00.569 --> 01:21:04.205
We got fifteen minutes to finish these connections
and then ten to get the hell out.


01:21:32.833 --> 01:21:36.436
- Bill...
- Where?


01:21:36.536 --> 01:21:37.704
Dunno, multiple points.


01:21:37.805 --> 01:21:38.671
Depth?


01:21:39.973 --> 01:21:42.809
- Above us I think.
- Then we proceed as planned.


01:21:44.543 --> 01:21:45.410
Tell George.


01:21:45.945 --> 01:21:47.713
Boy is on his own, we've got work to do.


01:22:40.864 --> 01:22:42.331
Shh. Shh.


01:23:13.361 --> 01:23:15.997
We don't have much time.
It's gonna fall.


01:23:17.732 --> 01:23:18.665
It'll hold.


01:23:19.867 --> 01:23:21.669
You two get the cable out.


01:23:22.253 --> 01:23:23.604
Just got a few more to do.


01:23:37.051 --> 01:23:40.320
Come to see how we win
a war like gentlemen, Jack?


01:23:41.521 --> 01:23:43.455
Depends what you mean by gentlemen sir.


01:23:51.798 --> 01:23:54.901
- How're we doing?
- Make sure the explosive's primed.


01:23:55.001 --> 01:23:57.635
It has to go off at six thirty exactly, alright?


01:23:59.105 --> 01:24:00.907
It goes off, no matter what.


01:24:07.847 --> 01:24:09.647
- Go on.
- Bill...


01:24:10.715 --> 01:24:11.850
...see you topside.


01:24:40.509 --> 01:24:42.813
- What the hell you doing?
- German saw me I killed him.


01:24:43.847 --> 01:24:44.882
I'm going to hell.


01:24:47.683 --> 01:24:51.888
The whole world's gonna fall in on us
here George. I need you out of here, now.


01:24:53.122 --> 01:24:55.992
- What about you?
- I've gotta stay and finish the wire.


01:24:56.659 --> 01:24:58.460
Oh no. Bill.


01:24:59.494 --> 01:25:01.897
Take this. This is our Peter's.


01:25:02.564 --> 01:25:04.100
Now listen to me George, listen to me.


01:25:05.067 --> 01:25:06.501
You're not going to hell.


01:25:08.904 --> 01:25:10.005
You were just protecting us.


01:25:12.706 --> 01:25:14.877
I should have protected your Charlie, I'm sorry.


01:25:16.411 --> 01:25:19.680
Now here we are.
And if we don't get these bombs set off


01:25:19.781 --> 01:25:23.418
this war'll go on and on,
before you know it our Pete will be Charlie's age.


01:25:25.987 --> 01:25:26.855
I can't have that.


01:25:32.060 --> 01:25:33.895
All this has to mean something.


01:25:37.798 --> 01:25:39.733
Some light has to leave these bloody tunnels.


01:25:40.566 --> 01:25:41.936
Alright?


01:26:36.123 --> 01:26:37.487
Ah come on Bill.


01:27:01.878 --> 01:27:02.745
Platoon!


01:27:03.611 --> 01:27:05.747
Fix.. bayonets!


01:27:19.527 --> 01:27:20.796
Shit! Shit!


01:27:27.169 --> 01:27:28.170
He'll have done it.


01:27:34.909 --> 01:27:36.011
No!


01:27:57.629 --> 01:27:58.832
Ah!


01:28:13.145 --> 01:28:14.279
Right.


01:28:14.380 --> 01:28:15.513
Done.


01:28:22.087 --> 01:28:23.688
What if Bill didn't make it?


01:28:25.323 --> 01:28:26.523
He gave us his orders.


01:28:30.660 --> 01:28:34.065
Oh Lord.
The shade on our right hand.


01:29:09.065 --> 01:29:09.999
George!


01:29:17.338 --> 01:29:19.041
I thought you'd bolted, son.


01:29:26.314 --> 01:29:27.215
Bill?


01:29:30.118 --> 01:29:31.219
He's dead.


01:30:01.147 --> 01:30:02.681
Get to a medic.


01:30:18.230 --> 01:30:20.765
Right. Come on lads.


01:30:21.933 --> 01:30:22.801
Let's go.


01:30:35.247 --> 01:30:37.248
<i>This morning at 6:30 a.m., an explosion</i>


01:30:37.348 --> 01:30:39.649
<i>the size of which
the world has never known,</i>


01:30:39.750 --> 01:30:41.318
<i>punctured German lines at Messines,</i>


01:30:41.418 --> 01:30:44.889
<i>allowing Allied troops to take
enemy trenches unscathed.</i>


01:30:44.989 --> 01:30:47.791
<i>The blast, so giant it was felt
back in Downing Street,</i>


01:30:47.892 --> 01:30:51.361
<i>was detonated through
underground bomb chambers dug...</i>


01:30:57.100 --> 01:30:59.736
I got the telegram yesterday,
there were no need to come.


01:31:03.106 --> 01:31:04.374
May I, anyway?


01:31:19.288 --> 01:31:21.723
There are things I'm supposed
to say in a situation like this.


01:31:23.792 --> 01:31:24.760
Such as hero...


01:31:26.494 --> 01:31:28.029
...selfless act...


01:31:30.499 --> 01:31:31.934
...patriot.


01:31:34.068 --> 01:31:35.403
But I'm not going to waste your time...


01:31:35.503 --> 01:31:37.205
Because we already know who William was.


01:31:37.939 --> 01:31:39.272
Didn't need a war to show it.


01:31:40.341 --> 01:31:42.843
A medal is just a fancy
piece of costume jewellery.


01:31:42.944 --> 01:31:44.844
And a letter from the King ain't worth...
Ears.


01:31:47.347 --> 01:31:49.450
Isn't worth the horseshit it's written on.


01:31:56.456 --> 01:32:01.895
I don't think I ever met, a more stubborn
pigheaded man than your husband,


01:32:01.995 --> 01:32:02.829
Mrs. Hawkin.


01:32:05.197 --> 01:32:07.166
And I don't think I've ever respected one more.


01:32:11.804 --> 01:32:12.471
Ah!


01:32:14.406 --> 01:32:15.474
I almost forgot.


01:32:19.945 --> 01:32:21.981
This little chap went everywhere with your father.


01:32:23.448 --> 01:32:26.952
It made him believe he could
achieve great things, and it did.


01:32:27.920 --> 01:32:28.987
It did..


01:32:30.121 --> 01:32:31.522
...save thousands of lives.


01:32:33.091 --> 01:32:34.359
Because he was yours.


01:32:36.961 --> 01:32:40.131
And now, he belongs back with you.


01:32:53.143 --> 01:32:54.076
Peter.


01:33:35.673 --> 01:33:38.533
The Messines explosion
was the most powerful ever recorded.


01:33:38.574 --> 01:33:41.336
The British Prime Minister heard
the detonation from London, 225 km away.


01:33:41.399 --> 01:33:43.655
The mines killed
more than 10,000 German soldiers.


01:33:43.711 --> 01:33:46.622
The enemy camp was invaded
by the Allies in less than 35 minutes.


01:33:46.692 --> 01:33:49.871
It was the very last tunnel of the Great War.

